    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ⚡ missed-call-text-back — START HERE\n\nEvery time someone calls and no one answers, this flow instantly texts the caller back so the lead isn't lost — and logs it for follow-up.\n\n```\nTwilio call webhook → Was Call Missed? → Format Call → Text Caller Back → Log Missed Call → Notify You\n```\n\n### Buyer setup checklist\n- [ ] **Twilio Call Webhook** → activate workflow, copy this node's *Production URL*\n- [ ] In **Twilio Console**, paste that URL into your number's *Call status changes* webhook (see the Twilio sticky →)\n- [ ] **Text Caller Back** → add Twilio creds, set `from` number, edit the message\n- [ ] **Log Missed Call** → pick your Google account + Sheet + tab (`Missed Calls`)\n- [ ] **Notify You** → optional; set your email or delete the node\n- [ ] Toggle **Active** and place a test call you don't answer\n\nAll credentials are placeholders — nothing sends until you connect your own.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 380,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "c1a2c3d4-0007-4a07-9007-stickyoverview",
      "name": "Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ⭐ #1 GOTCHA — wire Twilio correctly\n\nThis is the step everyone gets wrong.\n\n**Twilio Console → Phone Numbers → your number → Voice Configuration.**\n\n1. **\"A call comes in\"** must still route the call somewhere (your cell via a TwiML Bin `<Dial>`, a forwarding number, or voicemail). If this is empty the call fails before a status is ever reported.\n2. Scroll to **\"Call status changes\"** → set it to **HTTP POST** and paste the *Production URL* from the webhook node. **Save.**\n\nTwilio then POSTs every call's final status here. We keep only **missed** ones.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "c1a2c3d4-0008-4a08-9008-stickytwiliohk",
      "name": "Note - Twilio Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -200,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Was Call Missed?\n\nTwilio fires the status webhook several times per call (ringing, in-progress, completed…). We forward **only terminal missed statuses**:\n\n`no-answer` · `busy` · `failed` · `canceled`\n\nAnswered calls end as `completed` → **false** branch → nothing happens (no text). These four are terminal, so at most one fires per call = exactly one text-back, no duplicates.\n\nAlso reads `DialCallStatus` as a fallback if you used a `<Dial>` action callback instead.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "c1a2c3d4-0009-4a09-9009-stickyfilter00",
      "name": "Note - Filter",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        160,
        540
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Text Caller Back\n\nEdit the reply in the single **Message** field. Change `[Business Name]`; keep it short (one SMS segment is cheapest).\n\nSet your Twilio **From** number (full international, e.g. `+14155550100`) and add Twilio credentials.\n\n💡 **Auto-reply from the number they dialled:** set `From` to\n`={{ $('Format Call').item.json.calledNumber }}`\nso multi-number accounts always reply from the right line.\n\n`continueOnFail` is on, so logging + notify still run if a text can't send.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "c1a2c3d4-0010-4a10-9010-stickytwiliosm",
      "name": "Note - Text Back",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        480,
        540
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Log Missed Call & Notify\n\n**Log Missed Call** → set Document = your Sheet, Sheet = tab (default `Missed Calls`). Header row 1:\n\n`Time | Caller Number | Status`\n\nThis is your follow-up call list.\n\n**Notify You** is optional — set the destination email, or delete the node. Prefer Slack? Swap in a *Slack → Send Message* node and reuse `$('Format Call').item.json.*`.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "c1a2c3d4-0011-4a11-9011-stickylognotif",
      "name": "Note - Log & Notify",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        820,
        540
      ]
    }
